    "question": "¿Cuál es la diferencia estructural entre Possessive Adjectives y Possessive Pronouns?",
    "definition": "Possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) must always be followed by a noun (e.g., 'our meeting', 'her account'). Possessive pronouns (mine, yours, his, hers, its, ours, theirs) stand alone and replace the noun entirely (e.g., 'The final decision is theirs').",
    "analogy": "El adjetivo posesivo es un acompañante inseparable ('This is my file'); el pronombre posesivo es autosuficiente y va solo al final o como sujeto ('This file is mine').",
