    "definition": "Active Voice: The subject performs the action ('The banker reviewed the loan application'). Passive Voice: The subject receives the action, and the agent performing it is placed in a prepositional phrase or omitted ('The loan application was reviewed by the banker' or 'The forms were completed'). Formula: Form of 'To Be' + Past Participle.",
    "analogy": "En el sector legal y médico, la voz pasiva se usa cuando quien realiza la acción es obvio, desconocido, o cuando se desea enfocar la atención en el paciente o en el documento, evitando señalar culpas directas.",
    "code_example": "Active: 'The insurance company denied your claim.' (Sujeto realiza la acción)\nPassive: 'Your claim was denied (by the insurance company).' (Sujeto recibe la acción)\n---\nMedical: 'The surgery was performed successfully.' (Se resalta el procedimiento, no al cirujano)\nBanking: 'Your account was overdrawn.' (Cortesía: evita acusar directamente al cliente)",
