    "definition": "Subjects and verbs must match in number: singular subjects take singular verbs ('The policy covers all risks'), plural subjects take plural verbs ('The policies cover all risks'). Special rules: Subjects joined by 'and' take a plural verb ('The agent and the client discuss the terms'). Subjects joined by 'or' or 'nor' agree with the subject closest to the verb ('Neither the agent nor the clients are satisfied' vs 'Neither the clients nor the agent is satisfied').",
    "analogy": "Regla de la proximidad con 'Neither/Nor' y 'Either/Or': mira únicamente el sustantivo que está inmediatamente pegado al verbo para decidir si lleva 'is' o 'are'.",
